BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/swift-night-out-charlotte-3/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T201500
DTSTAMP:20260909T175038Z
CREATED:20260909T175038Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260909T175038Z
UID:10001796-1791139500-1791144900@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Swift Night Out (Charlotte)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF\, Mecklenburg Audubon Society\, and NCWF Charlotte Wildlife Stewards Chapter to meet the most spectacular aerial insectivores\, Chimney swifts. These birds spend almost their entire lives flying\, hunting insects\, and even bathing on the wing. Having lost much of their habitat to development\, chimney swifts now rely on brick mason chimneys for survival. As the sun goes down and the swifts make their way home for the night\, chat with local conservationists about chimney swift biology\, behavior\, and conservation. Discover their miraculous fall migration and observe swifts up close using scopes and binoculars. The night will culminate with the spectacle that is many hundreds of swifts chattering while swirling into a vortex before dropping into the chimney. Help us count the birds and contribute to their conservation efforts. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/swift-night-out-charlotte-3/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/SwiftNightOutHeader.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Index Ics": "https://arts.duke.edu/events/camerata-nordica/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_index_ics
X-SOURCE:Duke University

CATEGORIES:Arts
CATEGORIES:Utilities
CATEGORIES:Concert/Music
CATEGORIES:Main
CONTACT;X-BEDEWORK-UID=8a002cc9-9de3f0d7-019d-f89296c2-00006c0f:Williams\,
  Riley
CREATED:20260616T142629Z
DESCRIPTION:From one of Europe's premier chamber orchestras comes a group 
 of eight string players for an almost theatrical approach to chamber play
 ing. Standing in a semi-circle\, the self-conducted Camerata Nordica octe
 t is "in a class by itself in the way these players so perfectly negotiat
 e the very intricate\, most fiercely quick and complex sections" (Classic
 sToday.com).   \n\nGenius\, youth\, and a hint of irreverence - these are
  qualities shared by Mozart\, Mendelssohn\, and Shostakovich who wrote as
 tonishingly good works at a young age. A standout from Sweden's chamber s
 cene\, Camerata Nordica brings them together\, opening with a jocular rom
 p by Mozart\, while Mendelssohn's Octet serves as the anchor of the conce
 rt. Written by the composer at just 16\, the frolicsome\, high-energy Oct
 et\, spins dizzying interplay between eight independent voices. Considere
 d one of the masterworks of chamber music\, the Mendelssohn Octet inspire
 d the other octet on this program\, the blazing Op. 11 by 18-year-old Dmi
 tri Shostakovich.
DURATION:PT1H20M
DTSTAMP:20260818T211658Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261004T190000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260818T211658Z
