X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/stevens-creek-habitat-workday-waynesville-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T130000
DTSTAMP:20260805T153603Z
CREATED:20260805T153603Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260805T153603Z
UID:10001715-1791540000-1791550800@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:Stevens Creek Habitat Workday (Waynesville)
DESCRIPTION:Southern Appalachian Highlands Conservancy’s Stevens Creek property is situated on the Eastern edge of the Great Smoky Mountains National Park near the Cataloochee Valley. The Steven’s Creek property serves as an important wildlife corridor for the movement of numerous species headed north and south between Cataloochee and I-40\, as well as important habitat for the growing elk population. \nJoin NCWF’s Smoky Mountains Wilderness Watch Chapter alongside Southern Appalachian Highlands Conservancy for a habitat workday at Stevens Creek. We will focus the workday on managing open areas by removing tulip poplar saplings to encourage a wider variety of plant species and improve foraging habitat for elk and other wildlife. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/stevens-creek-habitat-workday-waynesville-2/
CATEGORIES:Featured
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncwf.org/wp-content/uploads/stevenscreekyes.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Naturalsciences": "https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/live-animal-feeding-ocean-habitat-5/2026-10-09/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:naturalsciences
X-SOURCE:NC Museum of Natural Sciences
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T104500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261009T110000
