X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050336Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54063933914023
DTSTART:20261010T160000Z
DTEND:20261010T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:​Beverages during the late 18th and early 19th century genera
 lly consisted of some form of alcohol\, even for the children. Fresh water
  could be hazardous to drink and with no refrigeration\, alcoholic beverag
 es were often consumed. One of these drinks\, a “small beer” could be 
 made at home and drank by the family. The ingredients were simple\, barley
  malt\, hops and water. It could be cooked over the daily fire and\nthough
  it didn’t have along shelf life\, it was easy enough to make in big or 
 small batches. Today we will go through the process of making a small beer
  and also serve a Ranquiem of cheese.\n\n“The New and Easy method of Coo
 kery” by Elizabeth Cleland\n“Seeking the historical cook” by Kay Mos
GEO:35.078;-80.882745
LOCATION:President James K. Polk Historic Site
SUMMARY:Historical Hearth Cooks Demonstration
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/historical-hearth-cooks-demo
 nstration-2043
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/copy-of-nc-the-beautiful-invasive-plant-purge-2268"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050336Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53692514965844
DTSTART:20261010T160000Z
DTEND:20261010T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:“Invasive” plants are introduced\, aggressively-growing pla
 nts that negatively impact local ecosystems. Join park staff at Haw River 
 State Park’s Iron Ore Belt Access to help remove these leafy invaders! \
 n\nTypical workdays start with paperwork for new volunteers (less than fiv
 e minutes) followed by a short hike to the work area where volunteers will
  receive instruction on how to identify the target species of the day. The
  rest of the time will be used on employing hands-on\, seasonally appropri
 ate techniques to remove invasive plants from the landscape\, helping to r
 estore the area for native plants and wildlife. \n\nAdvance registration i
 s required as supplies and space are limited. This opportunity is only ope
 n to volunteers ages 12 and up. Any volunteers under the age of 16 must be
  registered with and accompanied by an adult. \n\nVolunteers should wear l
 ong sleeves\, long pants\, and close-toed shoes. Please bring work gloves 
 and loppers or pruning shears if you have them\, but if not they will be p
 rovided (and you don't need to let us know in advance either way). Meet at
  the parking lot of the Iron Ore Belt Access.
GEO:36.23742;-79.785591
LOCATION:Haw River State Park - Iron Ore Belt Access 
SUMMARY:NC the Beautiful: Invasive Plant Purge
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/copy-of-nc-the-beautiful-inv
 asive-plant-purge-2268
CATEGORIES:Organizational
CATEGORIES:Volunteer Opportunities
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
CATEGORIES:Statewide Clean Up
END:VEVENT
