 age\, featuring two history talks: "Deep River: A Hundred Years Hence\, It
 s Voice Will Be Heard" by Ross A. Holt\, and "The First 250 Years of Frank
 linville" by Mac Whatley. Part of a larger event\, 4 p.m.-8:30 p.m.\, feat
 uring complimentary apple cider and pastries\, live weaving and spinning d
 emonstrations\, a community scarecrow competition\, a town time capsule ce
 remony and a sunset screening of the movie Pocahontas.
