X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/night-hike-history-of-land-conservation"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050336Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53947027482760
DTSTART:20261010T223000Z
DTEND:20261010T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join a park ranger for a guided hike along the Rumbling Bald Tr
 ail and discover how conservation\, recreation\, and community partnership
 s have shaped this special landscape.\n\nDuring the hike\, we’ll explore
  the role of ecotourism and how responsible outdoor recreation can connect
  visitors to the natural world while supporting the long-term protection o
 f our public lands. Learn about the history of land conservation efforts t
 hat helped shape the area and contributed to the formation of the state pa
 rk\, as well as the ongoing work to conserve and steward these important n
 atural resources.\n\nBring water\, comfortable shoes\, and a headlamp or f
 lashlight.
GEO:35.446778;-82.216898
LOCATION:Chimney Rock State Park - Rumbling Bald Access
SUMMARY:Night Hike - History of Land Conservation
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/night-hike-history-of-land-c
 onservation
