X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Naturalsciences": "https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/dueling-dinosaurs-sensory-friendly-mornings-2/2026-10-11/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:naturalsciences
X-SOURCE:NC Museum of Natural Sciences
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261011T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261011T120000
DTSTAMP:20261003T010348
CREATED:20260130T173156Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260130T173156Z
UID:119079-1791712800-1791720000@www.naturalsciences.org
SUMMARY:Dueling Dinosaurs Sensory Friendly Mornings
DESCRIPTION:Explore the Dueling Dinosaurs exhibit with reduced noise effects and smaller crowds. Please bring any noise-reducing headphones and fidgets you may need! A limited number of Sensory Friendly Bags are available for checkout at the front desk\, and a limited number of noise-reducing headphones are available to borrow at the exhibit. \nFree registration is not necessary but encouraged; if you register\, we’ll send reminder emails and resources about the exhibit so you can know before you go! \nPlease note that this is a self-guided tour of the exhibit space (not led by a museum educator)\, though you may interact with the research team in the SECU DinoLab! \nRegister Now! \n\nRecommended Audience\nAll ages\, particularly neurodivergent audiences. Children must be accompanied by adults. \n\nQuestions?\nIf you have any questions\, please contact the Coordinator of Accessibility\, Sam Frigerio\, at Accessibility@NaturalSciences.org or 919.707.9824.
URL:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/event/dueling-dinosaurs-sensory-friendly-mornings-2/2026-10-11/
LOCATION:Downtown Raleigh\, 11 West Jones Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Ages
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.naturalsciences.org/calendar/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/2024-04-15_DD-web.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Samantha%20Frigerio":MAILTO:Samantha.Frigerio@naturalsciences.org
GEO:35.7822735;-78.6395502
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Downtown Raleigh 11 West Jones Street Raleigh NC 27601 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=11 West Jones Street:geo:-78.6395502,35.7822735
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Ncwf": "https://ncwf.org/event/nc-deer-processing-workshop-alexander/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:ncwf
X-SOURCE:NC Wildlife Federation
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261011T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261011T140000
DTSTAMP:20260917T175412Z
CREATED:20260917T175411Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260917T175412Z
UID:10001800-1791712800-1791727200@ncwf.org
SUMMARY:NC Deer Processing Workshop (Alexander)
DESCRIPTION:Are you interested in learning to field dress and butcher a deer? Join National Wildlife Federation’s Artemis Sportswomen for a hands-on clinic. We will break down a deer carcass into primal cuts and discuss different practices for cooling and safe handling of meat in the field. \nArtemis ambassador Lisa Fierman is hosting this event in partnership with North Carolina Wildlife Federation and Southern Appalachian Highland Conservancy. The deer will be used as an educational tool for folks interested in learning how to process their own deer. Participants will be able to bring home some of the meat after attending the workshop.\n \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/nc-deer-processing-workshop-alexander/
CATEGORIES:Featured
END:VEVENT
