X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050336Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53796856318017
DTSTART:20261017T130000Z
DTEND:20261017T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:Step back in time and experience the history of eastern North C
 arolina during the 15th Annual John Lawson Legacy Days\, hosted by the Gri
 fton Historical Museum & Indian Village.\n\nThis multi-day living history 
 event brings the past to life through historical demonstrations\, reenacto
 rs\, guest speakers\, exhibits\, hands-on activities\, period crafts\, and
  educational programs exploring the people and events that shaped North Ca
 rolina. Visitors can learn about explorer and naturalist John Lawson\, Nat
 ive American history and culture\, colonial life\, early settlement\, and 
 the rich heritage of eastern North Carolina.\n\nThe 2026 celebration will 
 be especially meaningful as John Lawson Legacy Days coincides with the 50t
 h anniversary of the Grifton Historical Museum and the nationwide America2
 50 commemoration of the 250th anniversary of American independence.\n\nPro
 grams throughout the weekend will offer something for history lovers of al
 l ages\, from living history and demonstrations to special presentations a
 nd family-friendly activities. The weekend will also include opportunities
  to explore the museum and discover the fascinating history found right he
 re in eastern North Carolina.\n\nJoin us October 16–18\, 2026\, as we ce
 lebrate 15 years of John Lawson Legacy Days\, 50 years of preserving Grift
 on's history\, and 250 years of America's story.\n\nLocation: Grifton Hist
 orical Museum & Indian Village\, Grifton\, NC
GEO:35.368992;-77.432479
LOCATION:Grifton Historical Museum & Indian Village
SUMMARY:John Lawson Legacy Days
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/john-lawson-legacy-days
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
