X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/battlefields-to-backwoods-soldiers-shaping-applachia-celebrating-americas-250th"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050336Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52780900772707
DTSTART:20261017T160000Z
DTEND:20261017T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Transylvania Heritage Museum in Brevard for our 
 new exhibit celebrating America's 250th anniversary. Discover how Revolunt
 ionary War veterans\, including Transylvania County Patriots\, carried the
  spirit of liberty from battlefields into the rugged Appalachian frontier.
  Through artifacts\, stories and hands-on experiences - including our Revo
 lution Era Garden - explore the journey from conflict to community in the 
 mountains we call home!\n\nOpen Thursday through Saturday 12 p.m. to 4 p.m
 . Free and open to all. Donations accepted
GEO:35.234922;-82.737524
LOCATION:Transylvania Heritage Museum 
SUMMARY:Battlefields to Backwoods Soldiers Shaping Applachia  Celebrating A
 merica's 250th
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/battlefields-to-backwoods-so
 ldiers-shaping-applachia-celebrating-americas-250th
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/trail-to-victory-the-story-of-kings-mountain"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050336Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52506317161126
DTSTART:20261017T160000Z
DTEND:20261017T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Trail to Victory: The Story of Kings Mountain invites you on an
  unforgettable journey through time. Step into the heart of the 1780 Kings
  Mountain Campaign and witness the pivotal events that shaped the American
  Revolution.\n\nThis immersive museum experience leads you into the heart 
 of the harrowing events leading up to the October 7\, 1780 battle\, places
  you amidst the chaos of the conflict\, and allows you to experience the b
 attle's repercussions from the perspectives of both Patriots and British s
 oldiers.\n\nJoin us for three museum tours on Saturday\, October 17th\, st
 arting at 12:00 PM\, 1:30 PM\, and 2:30 PM. Tickets are available day of a
 t the Horn in the West Ticket Office.
GEO:36.208683;-81.669982
LOCATION:Hickory Ridge History Museum
SUMMARY:Trail to Victory: The Story of Kings Mountain
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/trail-to-victory-the-story-o
 f-kings-mountain
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
