SUMMARY:Free & Confidential HIV/STI Testing 
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261022T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261022T150000
DTSTAMP:20261003T050322Z
UID:7pe8achei4d9o6djftcff8o2fe_R20260723T170000@google.com__20261022
SEQUENCE:2
CREATED:20260629T193931Z
DESCRIPTION:Durham County’s “I Take Testing Seriously” Program (ITTS
 ) works with community partners and members alike to decrease rates of HIV
 \, Syphilis\, Hepatitis C\, Gonorrhea\, and Chlamydia. Our public health e
 ducators provide comprehensive sexual health services anywhere in Durham C
 ounty.<br><br>When folx attend testing services through the LGBTQ Center o
 f Durham\, they are able to receive: free and confidential HIV/STI screeni
 ngs\, PrEP referrals as needed\, and confidential counseling on next steps
 .<br><br>Specimens are sent to the NC State Lab  for testing where a 4<s
 up>th</sup> generation test is used.<br><br>Access to free barriers (inte
 rnal\, external) and lubrication is always readily available.<br><br>Our t
 ester can also answer questions about PrEP and provide initial steps in th
 e County's Quick Start program for PrEP. Stop in today!<br><br>Are you not
  ready to test? Stop in for an informational session.  All questions welc
 ome.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260930T225617Z
LOCATION:114 Hunt St\, Durham\, NC 27701\, USA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-SOURCE:LGBTQ Center of Durham
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/choosing-sides-the-catawba-nation-the-fight-for-independence"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050337Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53312428121557
DTSTART:20261022T140000Z
DTEND:20261022T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the Catawba Cultural Center\, Kings Mountai
 n Historical Museum is excited to present\, "Choosing Sides: The Catawba N
 ation & the Fight for Independence." This exhibit explores the critical ro
 le of the Catawba Nation\, also known as Yį Iswąre or “People of the R
 iver\,” in the American Revolutionary War\, particularly in the backcoun
 try regions of Tryon and Lincoln Counties. As skilled warriors\, guides\, 
 and allies of the Patriot cause\, the Catawba people defended their homela
 nd\, protected settler communities\, and contributed to pivotal battles. D
 espite the hardships of disease\, displacement\, and warfare\, the Catawba
  demonstrated extraordinary resilience. Their story is one of courage\, al
 liance\, and survival\, woven into the struggle for independence in the So
 uthern Campaign of the Revolution.\n\nThe exhibit will run from June 30\, 
 2026 until October 24\, 2026. Admission is Free!
GEO:35.239004;-81.342181
LOCATION:Kings Mountain Historical Museum
SUMMARY:Choosing Sides: The Catawba Nation & The Fight for Independence
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/choosing-sides-the-catawba-n
 ation-the-fight-for-independence
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
