DESCRIPTION:Join a Ranger and learn why the trees change color! Which tree 
 keeps its leaves all winter? If chlorophyll makes leaves green\, what make
 s green leaves become other colors? Learn the answers to these questions a
 nd tips for Winter Tree Identification during the hike on the Pump Station
  trail.\n\nAll children must be accompanied by an adult. Please be sure to
  dress appropriately for the weather\, wear hiking shoes\, and bring water
 !\n\nSpaces are limited\, and registration is required. To sign up\, call 
 (984) 250-1370 or email eno.river@ncparks.gov. Include the number of guest
 s in your party and a phone number where you can be reached if the event i
 s changed or canceled.
GEO:36.058541;-78.965815
LOCATION:Eno River State Park - Pump Station Access\, Lower Parking Area
SUMMARY:Changing Leaves Tree ID Hike
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/changing-leaves-tree-id-hike
 -401
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Outdoor & Recreation
END:VEVENT
