BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/educator-trek-got-elk"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050337Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53496784544118
DTSTART:20261023T180000Z
DTEND:20261023T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the NC Museum of Natural Sciences as they search for the m
 ajestic elk\, reintroduced to the Great Smoky Mountains National Park afte
 r an absence of more than 200 years. Observe and learn about elk biology\,
  while also exploring other facets of the Park’s ecosystem. Sample some 
 activities used to document the biodiversity of the Park. Participate in c
 itizen science data collection on snails and lichens. Discover how you can
  bring the excitement of field research into your classroom.\n\nCredit: 20
  contact hours toward CEUs or Criteria II/III for North Carolina’s Envir
 onmental Education Certification Program\n\nLodging: The workshop fee cove
 rs a two-night stay in a lodge in Lake Junaluska\, NC. Most rooms will be 
 double occupancy.\n\nTransportation: Participants can ride with the group 
 from Raleigh departing at 2pm or meet us at the lodging in Lake Junaluska 
 in the evening. Transportation will be in Museum vans.\n\nRegistration: Th
 is workshop is FULL\, please join our waiting list!\n\nThe full workshop f
 ee is due when you register and payment is via credit card. Registration f
 or most Educator Treks is on a first-come\, first-served basis. Treks fill
  quickly\, so register early! IF you find the program is full when you att
 empt to register\, please sign up for the waiting list! We frequently have
  turnover and often pull from the waiting list. We will let you know as so
 on as possible if a spot opens for you.\n\nAdditional Details:\n\nFee: $16
 0 (includes lodging\, some meals\, transportation\, and classroom resource
 s)Requirements: For educators (includes teachers\, administrators\, pre-se
 rvice or substitute teachers\; non-formal educators\; anyone working on th
 eir EE certification)Program Instructor(s): Megan Davis\, Rory McCollumAct
 ivity Level: Moderate (hiking up to two miles on uneven trails)\n Note: We
  do not want cost to be a barrier for any educator. If the cost of this wo
 rkshop would prevent your participation\, please reach out to Megan Davis.
  The cost of this workshop is subsidized by the Teacher Education fund at 
 the NCMNS.
LOCATION:Great Smoky Mountains National Park
SUMMARY:Sold Out: Educator Trek: Got Elk?
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/educator-trek-got-elk
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
