DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T233000
SUMMARY:🎆 ZincHouse 4th Anniversary Party + Fireworks 🍷🍺
DESCRIPTION:Discover Durham Together\nWine\, beer\, music\, food\, a beaut
 iful outdoor setting — and fireworks. Seems like a pretty solid excuse t
 o get a group together.\n\nWe’re heading to ZincHouse Winery & Brewery t
 o celebrate their 4th anniversary and hang out for the evening before capp
 ing the night with their anniversary fireworks show. 🎆\n\nZincHouse has
  a huge property with plenty of outdoor space to explore\, grab a drink\, 
 listen to music\, eat\, and hang out. We’ll meet up\, find a good home b
 ase for the group\, and enjoy the festivities together.\n\n🍷 Wine\n🍺
  Beer\n🍹 Drinks\n🍔 Food\n🎶 Music\n🎆 Fireworks show\n\nCome sol
 o or bring friends. New people are absolutely welcome — these events are
  meant to be an easy way to meet people without awkward organized icebreak
 ers or anything like that.\n\nWe’ll post our location once we’ve claim
 ed a spot so everyone can find us.\n\nGood drinks. Good people. Big firewo
 rks. See you there. 🎆
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/discover-durham-together/events/31679
 1789/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20261001T035901Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261001T035901Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardens": "https://gardens.duke.edu/event/japanese-tea-gathering-moon-viewing-tea/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardens
X-SOURCE:Sarah P. Duke Gardens
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T184500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261024T200000
DTSTAMP:20260915T130804Z
CREATED:20260908T195826Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260915T130804Z
UID:17883-1792867500-1792872000@gardens.duke.edu
SUMMARY:Japanese Tea Gathering: Moon Viewing Tea
DESCRIPTION:Join tea master Chizuko Sueyoshi and members of the Japanese Tea Practitioners of Durham for a moment of respite in the Duke Gardens teahouse\, where you will experience the centering calm of a Japanese tea gathering in the Urasenke tradition. Enjoy the aesthetics\, poetry and serenity of this rich tradition over an enticing bowl of whisked green tea and a Japanese confection.  Guests will be escorted on a 15-minute walk to the teahouse\, where seating is on the floor unless a chair is requested upon registration by emailing GardensEducation@duke.edu. For ages 12 and up. \nFee: $68; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Fees apply \nLocation: Onsite at Duke Gardens. \nAccessibility: This is a small group program that takes place indoors in a non-climate controlled space with floor seating\, in a location that requires outdoors traveling on a combination of paved and unpaved paths with some uneven surfaces and moderate inclines.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/japanese-tea-gathering-moon-viewing-tea/
LOCATION:Onsite at Duke Gardens – directions to follow
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs,Tea Ceremony
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/MAY25-PE_Sarah-P-Duke-Gardens_Japanese-Tea-Practitioners-of-Durham-2__StaceyVanBerkel-2.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/death-dying-seasonal-tour"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050337Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53922986345303
DTSTART:20261024T190000Z
DTEND:20261024T200000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special tour exploring the place of death in the 
 early 1800s. You will walk through the steps of a wake with a trained doce
 nt who will explain to you the community's response to death\, body prepar
 ation\, the wake\, burial and stone cutting techniques. The tour includes 
 a stop in the kitchen house and ends in the cemetery where you will learn 
 the unique history behind the Polk family cemetery.\n\nThis tour is design
 ed to be family friendly and suitable for all ages. All tour fees are paid
  on site prior to the start of the tour.\n\nTour guests can expect up to a
  1/4 mile of walking along some uneven ground. Please wear appropriate sho
 es and clothing for the weather. In the event of extreme heat\, cold or ra
 in\, the tour will be cancelled.
GEO:35.078;-80.882745
LOCATION:President James K. Polk Historic Site
SUMMARY:Death & Dying Seasonal Tour
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/death-dying-seasonal-tour
CATEGORIES:Exhibits & Tours
CATEGORIES:Guided Tours
END:VEVENT
