X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/history-at-high-noon-maco-light"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050337Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53498207984615
DTSTART:20261028T160000Z
DTEND:20261028T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Speaker: Holli Saperstein\, Executive Director\, Wilmington Rai
 lroad Museum\n\nJoin us for a spooky edition of History at High Noon as we
  explore the mystery of the Maco Light\, one of North Carolina’s most fa
 mous ghost stories! Reported for more than a century near old train tracks
  in Brunswick County\, this legend tells the story of a ghostly railroad c
 onductor named Joe Baldwin. After a tragic accident\, believers have claim
 ed to spot Baldwin’s spirit searching for his lost head. This talk will 
 examine the real history behind the tale and how the story became an impor
 tant part of local folklore\, attracting visitors and curiosity from acros
 s the country!\n\nFor questions\, please contact Stacey Smith at (919) 814
 -7032.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:History at High Noon: Maco Light
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/history-at-high-noon-maco-li
 ght
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
END:VEVENT
