X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Gardens": "https://gardens.duke.edu/event/mixed-media-floral-greeting-cards/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:gardens
X-SOURCE:Sarah P. Duke Gardens
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T120000
DTSTAMP:20260915T130805Z
CREATED:20260706T122638Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260915T130805Z
UID:17478-1793354400-1793361600@gardens.duke.edu
SUMMARY:Mixed-Media Floral Greeting Cards
DESCRIPTION:In this guided mixed-media workshop with Patricia Efunsade\, founder and creative director of SaKredJoi Art\, participants will create a series of botanically inspired greeting cards using a simple and approachable collage process. Begin by creating an 8.5 x 11-inch collage master sheet—a mixed-media process rooted in experimentation\, layering\, composition and storytelling through paper. Participants will then transform the paper into four unique handmade cards with designs that feature hand-cut flowers\, stems and leaves. Everyone will complete four finished greeting cards\, with the option to add personal words or sentiments. \nThis workshop is designed to be both relaxing and creatively engaging\, with a clear process that allows participants of all experience levels to leave with finished work that is ready to send or frame. All materials provided. \nFee: $45; 20% discount for Duke Gardens members with discount code. \nParking: Parking fees apply. \nLocation: Pelham-Cullen Classroom inside the Barnes Welcome Center. \nAccessibility: This program takes place seated in an indoor location accessible via paved surfaces and equipped with a hearing loop\, which transmits sound directly to hearing aids and cochlear implants with a T-coil setting. Accessible restrooms are available onsite.
URL:https://gardens.duke.edu/event/mixed-media-floral-greeting-cards/
LOCATION:Duke Gardens–Pelham-Cullen Classroom in the Barnes Welcome Center\, 420 Anderson Street\, Durham\, NC\, 27705\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adult Programs
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://gardens.duke.edu/wp-content/uploads/SakredJoi-greeting-card-by-Patricia-Efunsade.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_f511c08827b961733168ea93761e472cd12de35e813c3a73af3e44c56b7fe53d
SUMMARY:UU Justice NC’s Friday Action Hour
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261030T120000
DTSTAMP:20261003T050313Z
UID:1tvd180uho6fnokuhaj2c5h1k8_R20251107T160000@google.com__20261030
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20250729T151905Z
DESCRIPTION:11:00am-12:00pm: Unitarian Universalist Justice NC’s Friday 
 Action Hour. <a href="https://us06web.zoom.us/w/87452791684?_x_zm_rtaid=7M
 gmJB_hSsCKh3xUYHZrBA.1750590489156.1865f9b53934845e34cb2d06c2d1adc5&_x_zm_
 rhtaid=5#success" target="_blank"><u>Zoom here </u></a><br><u> </u><br><
 p>Since May of 2020\, North Carolina UUs and friends have gathered on Frid
 ays to take action and experience the joy and power of community. Every Fr
 iday at 11:00am we recap the past week and take action on the issues impac
 ting our state and country. And there is always great music to help us fee
 l the justice movement in our bones! ALL are welcome! We are also blessed 
 to be joined by Unitarian Universalists\, our beloved North Carolina justi
 ce partners\, and dear friends from outside our state (shout out to our We
 st Virginia fam!).</p><p>You can join us <strong>every Friday </strong>at 
 11:00 am via this <a href="https://us06web.zoom.us/meeting/register/tZMpcu
 uvpzosEtAhdqFHrSySSb6REM8wkPru">Zoom link</a>. And if you can't make it on
  Fridays\, you can still take action at any time - just check out our <a h
 ref="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Fwj6m0Qw4fAH_keuIoUNgdSWslBZzVgQ5
 NCgVPm_L-U/edit?tab=t.0" class="pastedDriveLink-0">Weekly action list</a>.
  And sign up for our <a href="https://secure.everyaction.com/QSBiJQ1YQEGwP
 O2KMIRIkQ2" target="_blank">Weekly Friday Action Hour Email</a> that inclu
 des a promo of the week's actions\, Zoom link\, and link to our Actions Go
 ogle Doc.</p><p><a href="https://www.uujusticenc.org/get-involved/friday-a
 ction-hour/">https://www.uujusticenc.org/get-involved/friday-action-hour/<
 /a> </p><u> </u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20251031T142802Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Durham Resistance (Virtual NC)
END:VEVENT
