BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/living-history-museum-days-at-hickory-ridge-history-museum-in-boone-nc"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050337Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52543890013505
DTSTART:20261114T150000Z
DTEND:20261114T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:We're going back to our roots.\n\nThis season\, Hickory Ridge H
 istory Museum proudly reintroduces Living History Museum Days\, a return t
 o the immersive\, hands-on spirit that once defined us as Hickory Ridge Li
 ving History Museum and “village”. On select days this summer\, the ca
 bins will come alive with the sights\, sounds\, and smells of 18th-century
  life in the North Carolina mountains.\n\nFrom open-hearth cooking and bla
 cksmithing to weaving\, spinning\, woodworking\, and frontier chores\, gue
 sts will experience a day in the life of the early settlers who called thi
 s region home. Our interpreters and volunteers will demonstrate traditiona
 l skills throughout the village\, inviting you to explore\, ask questions\
 , and connect with the everyday stories of Appalachian history.\n\nWhether
  you’re a longtime visitor or discovering us for the first time\, Living
  History Museum Days are your chance to step deeper into the past and to b
 e part of its future.\n\nInterested in volunteering or learning an 18th-ce
 ntury skill? We’re always looking for new hands to help bring the holler
  to life. Reach out to learn more about becoming part of SAHA family!
GEO:36.208683;-81.669982
LOCATION:Hickory Ridge History Museum
SUMMARY:Living History Museum Days at Hickory Ridge History Museum in Boone
 \, NC
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/living-history-museum-days-a
 t-hickory-ridge-history-museum-in-boone-nc
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/mining-society-merit-badge-workshop-2411"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050337Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53886882588667
DTSTART:20261114T150000Z
DTEND:20261115T070000Z
DESCRIPTION:Registered Scouts will have the opportunity to complete all req
 uirements needed to earn the “Mining in Society” merit badge at Reed G
 old Mine’s merit badge workshop.\n\nThe workshop begins with a PowerPoin
 t presentation and class time to finish the sections of the “Mining in S
 ociety” merit badge workbook. After completing the in-class portion\, Sc
 outs will be taken on a guided tour of the underground mine and learn abou
 t Reed Gold Mine’s history and learn more about the gold mining process.
  Following that\, weather permitting\, Scouts will be able to pan for gold
  in the outdoor panning area.\n\nThere is a $15 registration fee per Scout
 \, which includes the cost of the workshop\, tour\, and one panning ticket
  (weather permitting). Adult leaders and chaperones who wish to pan with t
 heir Scouts can purchase a panning ticket in the gift shop. Panning ticket
 s are sold on a first come\, first served basis and are $4.00 after tax. A
 dult leaders and chaperones may also buy a tour ticket if they’re intere
 sted in going on the guided tour of the underground mine. Tour tickets are
  $5.00 for adults 13 and older.\n\nIn 2026\, “Mining in Society” merit
  badge workshops will be offered May 9\, June 13\, July 11\, August 8\, Se
 ptember 12\, October 10\, and November 14. Each workshop begins at 10:00 a
 m and runs until 2:00 pm and is limited to 60 participants.\n\nRegistratio
 n form- https://tinyurl.com/5ubvkkkc\n\nFor more information and to schedu
 le\, contact Reed Gold Mine’s Education Coordinator\, Logan Stamper. He 
 can be reached by email at logan.stamper@dncr.nc.gov or by phone at (704) 
 721-4653.
GEO:35.285531;-80.466459
LOCATION:Reed Gold Mine
SUMMARY:Mining Society Merit Badge Workshop 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/mining-society-merit-badge-w
 orkshop-2411
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Workshops & Trainings
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Events 1 Ics": "https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/the-history-lake-james-from-native-lands-to-modern-recreation"}
X-SOURCE-ID:events_1_ics
X-SOURCE:NC Cultural Resources
DTSTAMP:20261003T050338Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53595964089280
DTSTART:20261114T150000Z
DTEND:20261114T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Lake James State Park for “The History of Lake Jam
 es: From Native Lands to Modern Recreation.” This program explores the r
 ich cultural and historical timeline of the settlement and development of 
 Lake James\, from the Indigenous tribes who first lived along the banks of
  the rivers\, to the development of hydroelectric generation that created 
 the lake as we know it\, and finally to today’s recreational opportuniti
 es within the state park and surrounding area. It’s a great way to learn
  how the landscape and its uses have transformed over time while enjoying 
 the natural beauty of Lake James.
GEO:35.760718;-81.882276
LOCATION:Lake James State Park\, Visitor Center Classroom
SUMMARY:The History Lake James: From Native Lands to Modern Recreation
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/the-history-lake-james-from-
 native-lands-to-modern-recreation
CATEGORIES:Education Programs
CATEGORIES:Lectures & Talks
END:VEVENT
