DESCRIPTION:Please join us for the June meeting of the America 250 NC Virtu
 al Book Club! We will be discussing Daughters of Green Mountain Gap by Ter
 i M. Brown on December 16 at 6p.\n\nThis historical fiction novel\, based 
 in North Carolina\, tells a story of generations of a women in one local f
 amily. As natural learning vs university education clash in the two older 
 women\, what is the third to think? Who will she follow? Is either path co
 rrect? \n\nPlease read the book prior to the discussion. We recommend borr
 owing from your local library. \n\nFree and open to the public. No members
 hip required. Come to whichever book talks spark your interest. \n\nMeetin
 g Link\n\nMore Information\n\nSign up for an Email Reminder
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Virtual Book Club: Daughters of Green Mountain Gap by Teri M. Brown
