UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_51825997978629
DTSTART:20261219T150000Z
DTEND:20261219T213000Z
DESCRIPTION:Prepare to celebrate and enjoy festive Scottish traditions for 
 New Year’s Eve (Hogmanay) and the Yule season. Enjoy speaking to Revolut
 ionary soldiers of the NC Highland and 71st Regiments\, listen to Gaelic m
 usic and storytelling\, learn about tartan history and see traditional Hog
 manay dishes made over an open fire\, and more. We encourage you to dress 
 in your family tartan or plaid! Food not available to the public. FREE. Al
 l ages welcome. Drop-in.
GEO:35.979741;-79.992174
LOCATION:High Point Museum
SUMMARY:Scottish Faire in Historical Park 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://events.dncr.nc.gov/event/scottish-faire-in-historical
 -park
CATEGORIES:Celebrations & Commemorations
CATEGORIES:Reenactments & Living History
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-ID:gcal_41d85e1478a55e3b4adbf2e4951c5be9f6e49241ac55a65427c71d252849bf1c
SUMMARY:Voter Registration in Durham
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261219T170000
DTSTAMP:20261003T050313Z
UID:0v72pvk68n3q4ur98thie5l4lh@google.com__20261219
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20260610T021016Z
DESCRIPTION:Please join Engaged Defenders for Democracy every Wednesday fr
 om 5-7pm and Saturday from 3-5 as we register voters in Durham. We will tr
 ain you and provide forms. We will be registering voters as well as talkin
 g about the important races in NC\, including Roy Cooper for US Senate and
  Anita Earls for NC Supreme Court.\n\nWe will meet at Common Market at 182
 1 Green St.\n\nThanks Diane and Barbara for being the Voter Registration l
